- <b>Espresso.</b> Two coats of cocoa brown that reads near-black indoors and chocolate in daylight. Brown is still in, as long as it leans espresso and not camel.
- <b>Black cherry.</b> A red-black with a violet flicker, and the quickest exit from burgundy fatigue.
- <b>Forest green.</b> Deep pine, closer to a spruce needle than a holiday ornament. Gloss, not shimmer.
- <b>Burnt copper.</b> A brown-orange metallic that works as a warmer take on silver, which is how <a href='https://www.thezoereport.com/beauty/november-nail-ideas'>The Zoe Report's November nail edit</a> frames it. A fine shimmer gel suits it better than foil.
- <b>Warm sheer nude.</b> Three thin coats of beige with a peach lean, built to look like your own nails on a very good day.
- <b>Plum or midnight purple.</b> The wildcard in a <strong>november nails</strong> palette, dark enough to pass as black until the light moves.

