## Which November Nail Finishes Look the Most Expensive?

Gloss is not what makes <strong>november nails</strong> look expensive. Softness is, and velvet nails lead the finishes that deliver it. Velvet nails are a magnetic-gel finish like cat-eye but with a softer, diffused glow, and aura nails and glazed gloss follow close behind.

- <b>Velvet.</b> A magnet held over the nail spreads the glow across the whole surface. Espresso and black cherry give the deepest, fabric-like result.
- <b>Cat-eye.</b> Cat-eye nails are a magnetic-gel finish that holds one sharp line of light across the nail and shifts as your hand moves. The full catalog lives in <a href='https://mirelleinspo.com/blog/fall-nails/fall-cat-eye-nails'>25 fall cat eye nails that feel expensive</a>.
- <b>Aura.</b> Aura nails are a soft, blurred halo of color, airbrushed or sponged, that glows at the center of the nail and fades outward. Copper over deep brown is the version to ask for.
- <b>Glazed gloss.</b> One pearl coat over a sheer beige, sealed with gel top coat. Wet-looking, never mirrored.
- <b>Jelly.</b> Translucent gel you can see through. Three coats of sheer black cherry build depth without turning opaque.
- <b>Matte.</b> Any deep shade under a matte top coat. Forest green and plum look best flat.

