## What Are the Best French Tips for November?

A classic French tip should be the easy choice, yet white at the tip is exactly what <strong>november nails</strong> reject. French tips are in style for November once the white goes: the best versions use a sliver of espresso, a dark cherry or green edge, or a gold rim. Micro French is a French manicure with a very thin line of color along the free edge, thinner than a classic tip, so the color reads as an outline and not a block.

- <b>Micro French in espresso.</b> A hairline of brown over a milky base. Quiet enough for any office.
- <b>Dark French.</b> Black cherry or forest green tips at full width on a sheer nude base.
- <b>Gold-edged.</b> A thin metallic gold rule along the tip edge only, over a neutral base.
- <b>Burnt orange.</b> A rust tip on a bare base. It is the only orange in this edit, and it works because it leans brown.
- <b>Black.</b> A crisp black tip on sheer pink. Graphic, not bridal.

