## What November Nail Art Feels Fresh, Not Pumpkin-Themed?

Art on <strong>november nails</strong> works best when the design stays tonal: one color family, one motif, nothing that belongs on a porch. Most of the six below need only one or two accent nails, so the rest of the set can stay plain.

- <b>Dark florals.</b> Black cherry petals hand-painted over espresso, on two accent nails.
- <b>Celestial.</b> Pinprick gold stars scattered over a plum base. No moon needed.
- <b>Polka dot.</b> Small cream dots on deep brown or black cherry. Retro without the costume.
- <b>Abstract art.</b> Loose, painterly swipes of copper over brown, with no two nails matching exactly.
- <b>Checkerboard.</b> Brown and cream squares on one or two nails. Clean lines take a steady liner brush and patience.
- <b>Croc or leopard accent.</b> Print on one nail only, in tonal browns. An accent, never a theme.

