## What Are the Best November Birthstone Nails?

Two stones share November: topaz and citrine. November birthstone nails are manicures that borrow the color of those stones, in sheer or jelly gel so the shade glows like the gem instead of sitting on top of it. Citrine is golden yellow, imperial topaz is warm orange-gold, and blue topaz runs from sky to deep blue.

- <b>Citrine.</b> One coat of sheer golden yellow over a milky base, kept low in saturation so it reads honey and not highlighter. Subtle enough for a birthday dinner.
- <b>Imperial topaz.</b> Amber-gold with a hint of rose in shimmer gel. Sits well beside burnt copper.
- <b>Blue topaz.</b> A clear, cool blue on a single accent nail among warm browns.
- <b>Topaz jelly.</b> Sheer amber built in three layers, the closest a polish gets to a stone's translucence.

