## Which <strong>November Nails</strong> Still Work in December?

A December manicure does not need red and glitter, whatever the party-season default says. Copper, forest green, a champagne tip, a glitter-edge French, and silver celestial art all work in November and still look right at a December party, because none of them depends on a fall motif.

- <b>Copper.</b> A glazed copper gel in fine shimmer, warm by day and celebratory under evening bulbs. A mirrored version is worth reading up on first: <a href='https://mirelleinspo.com/blog/fall-nails/fall-chrome-nails'>what chrome nails cost and how long they actually last</a>.
- <b>Forest green.</b> Deep pine in high gloss. With copper, it carries into December without reading Christmas, the same line <a href='https://www.womanandhome.com/november-nails/'>woman&amp;home's November edit</a> takes.
- <b>Champagne tip.</b> A pale gold tip over a milky base, the quickest December upgrade.
- <b>Glitter-edge French.</b> Fine glitter along the tip edge only, over a dark base. The sparkle outlines the nail instead of covering it.
- <b>Silver celestial.</b> A thin silver crescent and two stars on black or forest green.

