## How Do You Mix November Nail Colors Without Clashing?

A mixed set clashes because of the finish, not the color. To mix nail colors without clashing, keep one finish across every nail, pair one warm shade with one cool one, and stop at three colors.

- <b>Skittle set.</b> A skittle set gives each nail a different color. Keep all five in the same cream gel, say espresso, forest green, black cherry, plum, and copper.
- <b>Warm and cool pair.</b> Burnt copper on two nails against forest green on the rest. One warm, one cool, nothing else competing.
- <b>Gradient.</b> Espresso fading into black cherry from cuticle to tip, sponged on. Both share a red-brown base, so the blend stays clean.
- <b>Navy and beige.</b> Midnight navy beside a milky beige. The beige quiets the navy, which would otherwise look severe.
- <b>Three-color cap.</b> A dark, a neutral, and one metal. The fourth color is where a set stops looking intentional.

