## Give November Its Own Manicure

November is not the leftover stretch between pumpkin and glitter. It is the one month where a manicure can be properly considered, because no holiday is dictating it.

Treat it that way. Choose one dark shade, one soft finish, and one placement, then say all three out loud at the salon. "Espresso velvet, short oval, glossy top coat" is a complete instruction, and it is all a good nail tech needs.

Everything in this edit is built to be screenshotted, and most of it holds past the first week of December. Save the three looks you keep returning to. Leave the rest as a bank.

The best <strong>november nails</strong> are the ones you will still want on December 1.
